Reordered the checks so the common profile-lookup path falls through, and reused the already-invalid `type` as the fallback return to remove a separate invalid return branch. This avoids a taken branch on the typical decode path where `type` is unset and the profile field exists.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if ((type == FIT_UINT8_INVALID) &&
        (profile != NULL) &&
        (profileIndex < profile->numFields))
    {
        return profile->fields[profileIndex].type;
    }

    return type;
}
```